    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Invasive ductal carcinoma of the left breast, upper outer quadrant at 2 o&apos;clock, 2.4 cm on imaging; core biopsy grade 2, estrogen and progesterone receptor positive, HER2 negative, Ki-67 22 percent; clinical stage T2 N0 (cT2 cN0 M0); synthetic modern counterpart of the documented 1960 breast cancer, which was not disclosed to her</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>C50.412</td><td>S — Synthetic tumor details, stage, and treatment; the breast lumps, the 1960 operation, and the nondisclosure are documented (D), but no tumor details from her lifetime are used.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Estrogen receptor positive status of the breast cancer (ER 95 percent, PR 80 percent)</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z17.0</td><td>S — Synthetic receptor result; no receptor status from her lifetime is known.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>New firm lump in the upper outer quadrant of the left breast, found two weeks ago; clinically suspicious; diagnostic imaging and biopsy booked</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>N63.21</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting concern at the index visit, superseded by the biopsy diagnosis; the lumps in the left breast in early 1960 are documented (D).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Duodenal ulcer found at endoscopy seven weeks ago, with Helicobacter pylori on biopsy; treated with 14 days of bismuth quadruple therapy and completing eight weeks of omeprazole; test of cure planned</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>K26.9</td><td>S — Synthetic modern ulcer; it echoes the ulcer among her documented illnesses, which the sources do not date.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Primary osteoarthritis of both knees, mild, with stiffness after long walks on the shore</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>M17.0</td><td>S — Synthetic condition; it is not linked to the documented word arthritis, which she may have used to keep her cancer private.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

